# SPA fallback for /<slug> deep links (e.g. /Sikhio). Rules are evaluated
# top-down; the first match wins. Static assets and /api/* Functions
# are matched first so the wildcard at the bottom only catches paths
# that have no other match — exactly the case for a bare place slug.
# The URL bar keeps /Sikhio so the link is shareable.
#
# IMPORTANT: Cloudflare Pages 200-rewrites can outrank bare static files at
# the site root. Without these pass-throughs, /sw.js was served as ops.html
# (85197 bytes of HTML) and service-worker registration silently failed —
# returning visitors stayed on stale shells. Keep every root asset listed.
/css/*   /css/:splat  200
/js/*    /js/:splat   200
/img/*   /img/:splat  200
/fonts/* /fonts/:splat 200
/geo/*   /geo/:splat  200
/vendor/* /vendor/:splat 200
/photos/* /photos/:splat 200
/sw.js                  /sw.js                  200
# Never register /sw.js?v=… — query strings miss this rule and SPA-fallback to ops.html.
/manifest.webmanifest   /manifest.webmanifest   200
/robots.txt             /robots.txt             200
/sitemap.xml            /sitemap.xml            200
/icon.svg               /icon.svg               200
/index.html             /index.html             200
/ops.html               /ops.html               200
# Catch-all: any other unmatched path is treated as a place slug and
# served by the operator dashboard. bootCityFromSlug() in main.js
# reads the path and pins the city via /api/place/slug/:splat.
/*  /ops  200
